# Normalize text files, then pin line endings per platform.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must keep LF: CRLF makes Linux fail with "bad interpreter".
*.sh text eol=lf

# Batch files are stored with CRLF bytes and never converted.
#
# `text eol=crlf` is not enough. It normalises to LF inside the repository and
# only restores CRLF on checkout, so a ZIP downloaded from the forge, which
# does no such conversion, hands out LF batch files. cmd.exe resolves `call
# :label` by byte offset assuming CRLF, and on an LF file it silently fails to
# find labels further down with "cannot find the batch label specified".
# Marking them -text keeps the bytes verbatim everywhere.
*.bat -text

*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
